Z||000008||LarryB||08-20-2001||01:15 PM||||GIF is a lossless format, so if you're manipulating 8-bit (GIF is also 8-bit) images it yields better results.  PNG yields better quality 24-bit pictures than JPEG because it is also lossless, but at the expense of larger files. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>why use GIF? JPG quility is so much better for not much more space... only advantages with GIF is you can animate them... JPG u can simply use PIP</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
